event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":93,"item_id":"rs_0f382c1bbe15a8f9016acb982f7ae087d2861795b7f8500e57","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI need to create a simple implementation of server-side rendered (SSR) forms using native JavaScript. The goal is to keep it straightforward, maybe without requiring textbox labels. I want to ensure that the form redirects and provides an alert on submission. An accessible button should work for submitting the form, which will use a URL-encoded POST route for project creation. I should also think about testing with a temporary database to check health persistence during implementation."}

